    { "path": "Champions of Krynn/SOUND.DAX", "category": "data", "label": "SOUND (DOS sound bank)", "decode": false, "note": "One block (id 1), 14,064 bytes. Round 34 R6 (docs/engine/research/cok-sound-bank.md): the block's own first word is a driver-verified stream-start pointer (0x007d = 125, seeded into the resident driver's tick cursor by `mov ax, es:[0]` at install time), and decoding the running-status grammar from 125 runs to a literal 0xFC terminator with 0 malformed bytes -- 11,090 real events plus the decoder's own end marker. It segments into 14 streams, 3 of which are large, balanced, five-voice passages (4,801 / 1,141 / 5,132 events, Note-On and Note-Off within 6 of each other in each) -- the shape of music, not one-shot effects. Against a histogram-preserving shuffle of all 814 corpus sources the null's best is 368 events and no source terminates cleanly at all, so this block ranks #1 of 814 by >30x. THIS IS A DECODE CENSUS, NOT PLAYBACK: nothing in the engine renders these events to audio, and the dashboard row says so. The web build's Champions music is the Amiga path, which is unrelated to this file." }
